# Cloudiator

You are building a Mac Mini M4 24GB inference appliance. `PLAN.md` wins over blogs.

- One phase per chat. Stop at that phase's definition of done.
- Do not use Docker for Ollama/MLX. Official Ollama.app, bind worker to `127.0.0.1:8080` only.
- `uvicorn --workers 1` always. `metal_lock` is in-process; a second worker means a second scheduler.
- `OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=2`: slot 1 = one generative model, slot 2 = `nomic-embed-text` only.
- Always send an explicit `keep_alive`: `-1` for the hot model and embedder, `0` for everything else.
- Exclusive slot work goes in `try/finally`: kill orphans, reload the hot model, release the lock.
- Never tunnel or expose `11434`. Never put inference in Netlify Functions.
- One Metal-heavy model at a time. Do not `ollama pull` 70B, 120B, or default-hot 27B. `gpt-oss:20b` is Phase E only.
- Python 3.11 arm64 only. Abort on x86_64/Rosetta.
- FastAPI owns the tool loop: max 8 iterations, 75s budget, scope re-checked every call.
- Vision `image_url` is SSRF-exposed: https/data only, resolve DNS, block private ranges, downscale to 1024px.
- Admin and dashboard are behind Cloudflare Access. No shared password, no login form.
- Libraries first (OCR, DuckDB, charts, Pillow). Models last. No unrestricted `eval`.
- DuckDB is locked down by configuration (`enable_external_access=false`), not by a keyword regex.
- Salesforce keys: `stream=false`, `max_tokens=512`, Apex timeout 120000, jobs for FLUX/20B, artifact URLs never base64.
- Do not commit `.env` or API keys. Artifacts stay under `~/Cloudiator/`, not git.
